  <p class="kick">Brain training in the age of AI</p>
  <h1>Applied philosophy: Plato's paths</h1>
  <p class="sub">Slow reading of the first Greek philosophers and of Plato's <em>Parmenides</em> — the most demanding text of Western thought — in a small group, with a guide and a method.</p>
  <p>Eight 75-minute sessions on Zoom, groups of 4–8, minimum lecturing, maximum practice. No prior philosophical training required — only attention and openness to start thinking again from the very beginning of metaphysics.</p>
  <p>The English-language stream is being prepared. Meanwhile, the <a href="/map">filiation map of the Parmenides</a> (56 authors, in Russian) and the <a href="/polygons">three non-Western polygons</a> are open to everyone.</p>
  <p><a class="btn" href={TELEGRAM} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Message me on Telegram</a></p>
</Base>
